{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinring/tmlanguage/master/tmlanguage.json",
  "name": "AvaLang",
  "scopeName": "source.avalang",
  "fileTypes": ["ava"],
  "patterns": [
    { "include": "#comments" },
    { "include": "#line-continuation" },
    { "include": "#extern-block" },
    { "include": "#class-declaration" },
    { "include": "#func-declaration" },
    { "include": "#import-statement" },
    { "include": "#member-modifiers" },
    { "include": "#async-modifier" },
    { "include": "#await-keyword" },
    { "include": "#keywords-control" },
    { "include": "#keywords-other" },
    { "include": "#type-annotation" },
    { "include": "#operators-logical" },
    { "include": "#language-constants" },
    { "include": "#this-reference" },
    { "include": "#stdlib-namespaces" },
    { "include": "#property-access" },
    { "include": "#strings" },
    { "include": "#numbers" },
    { "include": "#dict-literal" },
    { "include": "#named-argument" },
    { "include": "#function-call" },
    { "include": "#operators" },
    { "include": "#punctuation" }
  ],
  "repository": {

    "comments": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "comment.line.number-sign.avalang",
          "begin": "#",
          "end": "$",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "match": "\\b(TODO|FIXME|NOTE|HACK|XXX)\\b",
              "name": "keyword.other.comment-tag.avalang"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "line-continuation": {
      "match": "\\\\\\s*$",
      "name": "constant.character.escape.line-continuation.avalang"
    },

    "import-statement": {
      "match": "\\b(import)\\b\\s*((?:[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*(?:\\.[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)*))?\\s*(?:\\b(as)\\b\\s*([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*))?",
      "captures": {
        "1": { "name": "keyword.control.import.avalang" },
        "2": { "name": "entity.name.namespace.avalang" },
        "3": { "name": "keyword.control.import.avalang" },
        "4": { "name": "entity.name.namespace.alias.avalang" }
      }
    },

    "extern-block": {
      "begin": "\\b(extern)\\b\\s*",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": { "name": "keyword.control.extern.avalang" }
      },
      "end": "\\b(end)\\b",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": { "name": "keyword.control.extern.avalang" }
      },
      "patterns": [
        { "include": "#comments" },
        {
          "comment": "El alias de modulo (`extern \"lib\" as Alias`) es el unico `as X` de este bloque que va pegado directamente al STRING que abre el extern -- de ahi el lookbehind. Los `as Type` de un `externParam`/`returnType` (Fase 16 del plan de tipos, ej. `func Sleep(ms as int)`, `func GetTickCount() as int`) van pegados a un NAME o a `)`, nunca a un STRING, asi que quedan afuera de este match y los resuelve #type-annotation mas abajo en este mismo arreglo.",
          "match": "(?<=\")\\s*\\b(as)\\b\\s*([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": { "name": "keyword.control.extern.avalang" },
            "2": { "name": "entity.name.namespace.alias.avalang" }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b(func)\\b\\s*([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": { "name": "storage.type.function.avalang" },
            "2": { "name": "entity.name.function.avalang" }
          }
        },
        { "include": "#type-annotation" },
        { "include": "#strings" },
        { "include": "#punctuation" },
        {
          "match": "\\*",
          "name": "keyword.operator.splat.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*",
          "name": "variable.parameter.avalang"
        }
      ]
    },

    "class-declaration": {
      "match": "\\b(class)\\b\\s+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)(?:\\s*(:)\\s*([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*))?",
      "captures": {
        "1": { "name": "storage.type.class.avalang" },
        "2": { "name": "entity.name.type.class.avalang" },
        "3": { "name": "keyword.operator.heritage.avalang" },
        "4": { "name": "entity.other.inherited-class.avalang" }
      }
    },

    "func-declaration": {
      "match": "\\b(func)\\b\\s*([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)?\\s*(?=\\()",
      "captures": {
        "1": { "name": "storage.type.function.avalang" },
        "2": { "name": "entity.name.function.avalang" }
      }
    },

    "member-modifiers": {
      "match": "\\b(static|private)\\b",
      "name": "storage.modifier.avalang"
    },

    "async-modifier": {
      "comment": "`async` de asyncFuncDeclaration ('async' funcDeclaration, ver AvaLang.g4). Mismo molde sintactico que memberModifier (static/private) delante de funcDeclaration, pero con su propio scope storage.modifier.async.avalang -- el estandar en gramaticas TextMate (JS/TS: storage.modifier.async) para que los temas existentes lo coloreen distinto de static/private sin tocar member-modifiers.",
      "match": "\\basync\\b",
      "name": "storage.modifier.async.avalang"
    },

    "await-keyword": {
      "comment": "`await` de awaitAtom ('await' expr, dentro de primary -- ver AvaLang.g4). Solo es valido dentro del cuerpo de un asyncFuncDeclaration; eso lo valida el compilador (Compiler::in_async_func_), no la gramatica ni este resaltado. Va antes que #function-call en el arreglo de patterns de la raiz para que 'await(x)' (sin espacio) no se interprete como una llamada a una funcion llamada 'await'.",
      "match": "\\bawait\\b",
      "name": "keyword.control.flow.await.avalang"
    },

    "keywords-control": {
      "match": "\\b(if|then|elif|else|end|while|for|in|try|catch|finally|return|break|continue|pass|raise|select|case|to|is)\\b",
      "name": "keyword.control.avalang"
    },

    "keywords-other": {
      "match": "\\b(local|base|yield)\\b",
      "name": "keyword.other.avalang"
    },

    "type-annotation": {
      "comment": "`as Type` de AvaLang_Plan_Sistema_de_Tipos.md: anotacion de variable (`age as int`, con o sin `= expr`), de parametro (`func f(a as int)`, incluye `externParam`) y de retorno (`returnType`, tanto en `func` como en las dos formas de lambda). Deliberadamente NO incluye el `as` de `import ... as Alias` ni el de `extern \"lib\" as Alias` -- esos ya tienen su propio resaltado mas especifico (namespace/alias) en #import-statement y dentro de #extern-block, que van antes en el arreglo `patterns` de la raiz y ya consumen esa `as X` como parte de un match mas largo; y el `as` inmediatamente despues del STRING que abre un `extern` esta ademas excluido acá con un lookbehind, para que esta regla no lo vuelva a capturar como si fuera un tipo cuando aparece dentro del propio cuerpo de #extern-block (que sí incluye esta regla, para los `as Type` de sus `externParam`/`returnType`).",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "(?<!\"\\s*)\\b(as)\\b\\s*\\b(int|float|bool|string)\\b",
          "captures": {
            "1": { "name": "keyword.control.as.avalang" },
            "2": { "name": "storage.type.primitive.avalang" }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "(?<!\"\\s*)\\b(as)\\b\\s*([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": { "name": "keyword.control.as.avalang" },
            "2": { "name": "entity.name.type.avalang" }
          }
        }
      ]
    },

    "operators-logical": {
      "match": "\\b(and|or|not)\\b",
      "name": "keyword.operator.logical.avalang"
    },

    "language-constants": {
      "match": "\\b(true|false|nil)\\b",
      "name": "constant.language.avalang"
    },

    "this-reference": {
      "match": "\\bthis\\b",
      "name": "variable.language.this.avalang"
    },

    "stdlib-namespaces": {
      "comment": "Namespaces del modulo nativo 'system' (runtime/avalang/src/builtins/system_module.cpp): System, System.Console, System.DateTime, System.Environment, System.IO.{File,Directory}, System.Diagnostics.Process. Solo colorea cuando el identificador va seguido de un punto (uso como namespace), para no pisar variables sueltas que se llamen igual.",
      "match": "\\b(System|Console|DateTime|Environment|IO|File|Directory|Diagnostics|Process)\\b(?=\\s*\\.)",
      "name": "support.class.avalang"
    },

    "property-access": {
      "match": "(?<=\\.)\\s*\\b([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)\\b(?!\\s*\\()",
      "captures": {
        "1": { "name": "variable.other.property.avalang" }
      }
    },

    "numbers": {
      "match": "\\b[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\b",
      "name": "constant.numeric.avalang"
    },

    "dict-literal": {
      "name": "meta.structure.dictionary.avalang",
      "begin": "\\{",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "0": { "name": "punctuation.curlybrace.open.avalang" }
      },
      "end": "\\}",
      "endCaptures": {
        "0": { "name": "punctuation.curlybrace.close.avalang" }
      },
      "patterns": [
        { "include": "#comments" },
        {
          "match": "\\b([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)\\b\\s*(:)(?!:)",
          "captures": {
            "1": { "name": "support.type.property-name.avalang" },
            "2": { "name": "punctuation.separator.key-value.avalang" }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "(\"(?:[^\"\\\\\\r\\n]|\\\\[btnr\"'\\\\])*\"|'(?:[^'\\\\\\r\\n]|\\\\[btnr\"'\\\\])*')\\s*(:)(?!:)",
          "captures": {
            "1": { "name": "string.quoted.avalang support.type.property-name.avalang" },
            "2": { "name": "punctuation.separator.key-value.avalang" }
          }
        },
        { "include": "$self" }
      ]
    },

    "named-argument": {
      "match": "(?<=[(,])\\s*\\b([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)\\b(?=\\s*=(?!=))",
      "captures": {
        "1": { "name": "variable.parameter.avalang" }
      }
    },

    "function-call": {
      "match": "\\b([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9]*)\\b(?=\\s*\\()",
      "captures": {
        "1": { "name": "entity.name.function.avalang" }
      }
    },

    "escapes": {
      "match": "\\\\[btnr\"'\\\\]",
      "name": "constant.character.escape.avalang"
    },

    "strings": {
      "patterns": [
        { "include": "#fstring" },
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.double.avalang",
          "begin": "\"",
          "end": "\"",
          "patterns": [{ "include": "#escapes" }]
        },
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.single.avalang",
          "begin": "'",
          "end": "'",
          "patterns": [{ "include": "#escapes" }]
        }
      ]
    },

    "fstring": {
      "name": "string.interpolated.avalang",
      "begin": "\\$\"",
      "end": "\"",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "0": { "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.avalang" }
      },
      "endCaptures": {
        "0": { "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.avalang" }
      },
      "patterns": [
        { "include": "#escapes" },
        {
          "match": "\\{\\{|\\}\\}",
          "name": "constant.character.escape.avalang"
        },
        {
          "name": "meta.embedded.expression.avalang",
          "begin": "\\{",
          "end": "\\}",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "0": { "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.avalang" }
          },
          "endCaptures": {
            "0": { "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.avalang" }
          },
          "patterns": [
            { "include": "#comments" },
            { "include": "#async-modifier" },
            { "include": "#await-keyword" },
            { "include": "#keywords-control" },
            { "include": "#keywords-other" },
            { "include": "#operators-logical" },
            { "include": "#language-constants" },
            { "include": "#this-reference" },
            { "include": "#stdlib-namespaces" },
            { "include": "#property-access" },
            { "include": "#strings" },
            { "include": "#numbers" },
            { "include": "#dict-literal" },
            { "include": "#named-argument" },
            { "include": "#function-call" },
            { "include": "#operators" },
            { "include": "#punctuation" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "operators": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "\\+=|-=|\\*=|/=|%=|//=",
          "name": "keyword.operator.assignment.compound.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "==|!=|<=|>=|<|>",
          "name": "keyword.operator.comparison.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "\\+\\+|--",
          "name": "keyword.operator.increment-decrement.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "=>",
          "name": "storage.type.function.arrow.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "\\*\\*",
          "name": "keyword.operator.arithmetic.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "//",
          "name": "keyword.operator.arithmetic.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "[+\\-*/%]",
          "name": "keyword.operator.arithmetic.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "=",
          "name": "keyword.operator.assignment.avalang"
        },
        {
          "match": "\\.",
          "name": "punctuation.accessor.avalang"
        }
      ]
    },

    "punctuation": {
      "patterns": [
        { "match": ",", "name": "punctuation.separator.comma.avalang" },
        { "match": ";", "name": "punctuation.terminator.statement.avalang" },
        { "match": ":", "name": "punctuation.separator.colon.avalang" },
        { "match": "[()]", "name": "punctuation.parenthesis.avalang" },
        { "match": "[\\[\\]]", "name": "punctuation.squarebracket.avalang" },
        { "match": "[{}]", "name": "punctuation.curlybrace.avalang" }
      ]
    }

  }
}
